%N A398700 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} sigma(k)/(k^2*(k+1)), where sigma(k) = A000203(k) is the sum of divisors of k.
%C A398700 This constant appears in the asymptotic formula for the function A398698(n)/A398699(n).
%H A398700 Jing Ma and Huayan Sun, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11139-022-00588-y">On a sum involving certain arithmetic functions and the integral part function</a>, The Ramanujan Journal, Vol. 60, No. 4 (2023), pp. 1025-1032; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11139-026-01336-2">Correction</a>, ibid., Vol. 69 (2026); <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.02924">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2109.02924 [math.NT], 2021; <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361229857">ResearchGate link</a>. See Theorem 1, p. 1027.
%F A398700 Equals 1/2 + Sum_{k>=3} (-1)^k * (D(k) - 1), where D(s) = zeta(s-1)*zeta(s) is the Dirichlet g.f. of sigma.
%e A398700 1.261130385915375187861714822618520064585099351211146...
%o A398700 (PARI) suminf(k = 3, (-1)^(k+1) * (zeta(k-1)*zeta(k) - 1)) + 1/2
%Y A398700 Cf. A000203, A398534, A398698, A398699.
%K A398700 nonn,cons
%O A398700 1,2
%A A398700 _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 07 2026
